WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.463
This is the deliverable.

2
00:00:01.463 --> 00:00:05.623
For any period, the code verifies
every package, checks the chain,

3
00:00:05.623 --> 00:00:09.235
confirms the windows cover
the whole period with no gap,

4
00:00:09.235 --> 00:00:12.062
and writes a summary
laid out against Gate 4.

5
00:00:12.062 --> 00:00:14.247
It's clear about who decides what:

6
00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:18.618
the authorizing official accepts
residual standing privilege,

7
00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:21.936
the ISSO judges the
elevations, and one criterion,

8
00:00:21.936 --> 00:00:26.387
retiring old group policy settings,
simply isn't a privileged read.

9
00:00:26.387 --> 00:00:30.729
The sample workflow runs daily with
a federated sign-in and no secret,

10
00:00:30.729 --> 00:00:33.624
and assembles last month's
period on the first.

11
00:00:33.624 --> 00:00:36.700
Six-hourly runs need
only a shorter schedule.
